<small>A Song of degrees.</small><br /><sup><b>1</b></sup> Unto thee lift I up mine eyes, O thou that dwellest in the heavens.<br />
<sup><b>2</b></sup> Behold, as the eyes of servants <i>look</i> unto the hand of their masters, <i>and</i> as the eyes of a maiden unto the hand of her mistress; so our eyes <i>wait</i> upon the LORD our God, until that he have mercy upon us.<br />
<sup><b>3</b></sup> Have mercy upon us, O LORD, have mercy upon us: for we are exceedingly filled with contempt.<br />
<sup><b>4</b></sup> Our soul is exceedingly filled with the scorning of those that are at ease, <i>and</i> with the contempt of the proud. <br />
